Z||000000||chris6878||12-03-1999||12:57 PM||||Hey...<P>Everything is done to the engine and i solved my wiring problem (had a ground)...<BR>Well.. when i got to turn the key.. everything is fine.. but when i turn it on around to start the engine.. nothing happens.. the battery is full charged.. the lights dont even flicker or anything when i am attempting to start the engine..  i must have forgot to hook something up...   all my gauges and stuff come on like there suppose to.. but the engine wont turn..??    I got under the car and tried started it by crossing the starter,  the engine turns but i dont think its getting any power to the coil and such because it wont turn by the  key...  Anyone know what it could be.??||||reg||9
Z||000001||William Federle||12-03-1999||01:00 PM||||It's just a thought, but if you have a standard transmission and your clutch switch<BR>isn't activated (by you pushing the clutch<BR>all the way in) then it won't start.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||12-03-1999||01:11 PM||||I just had to deal with a Bad Neutral Start Switch last weekend and boy was I pissed.  It took me like 4 hours to narrow it down to that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||chris6878||12-03-1999||01:41 PM||||My transmission is an automatic ..... Where is the Neutral Start Switch ? Is it the plug in on the side of the tranny?   <P><BR>Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000004||Phaeton||12-04-1999||03:20 PM||||On the rear top of the transmission where the shift cable attaches to the shift shaft ther is a switch box.  With the shifter in neutral there is an alignment hole that a 3/32 bit should fit in.  If the bit does not go 3/8" into the hole loosen the two bolts holding the switch in place and rotate it until the bit drops in, then tighten the switchbox down.  ||||reg||1
